    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Kirkland Lake Family Entertainment Series: Silly Billy (Kirkland Lake, ON)"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p class='p1'><i>Silly Billy</i> is on tour this fall! As we make our way through the beautiful landscapes of northern Ontario, we are excited to visit Kirkland Lake for the first time.</p> <p class='p1'><i>Silly Billy</i> is a story about a rare white buffalo unhappy with his uniqueness, who goes on a quest to find the magical Unicorn in the hopes of emulating this mythical creature. Through adventures, obstacles, misunderstandings and mishaps, Billy discovers his own self-worth, embraces his difference, and takes his place alongside the Unicorn as the legendary great white buffalo of the plains. This iteration of <i>Silly Billy</i> will feature Chimera artists Waawaate Fobister stepping into the role of Billy and Emma Curtis resuming her role as the Unicorn.</p> <p><a href='https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/silly-billy-presented-by-klfes-tickets-1671967904009?aff=ebdsoporgprofile'>Ticket information for Silly Billy</a></p> <p>6:30 PM at the Northern College Auditorium (140 Government Road East)</p> "
      }
    ],
